{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 40,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Before we get started, we wanted \nto let you know there’s some new  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2600,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "limited edition Merch for sale at the Merch store."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5800,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meet Alice and Bob, famous explorers of the\nabstract landscape of theoretical physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11280,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Heroes of the gerdankenexperiment—the thought\nexperiment—whose life mission is to find"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17560,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "contradictions in the deepest layers of our\ntheories and so bring us deeper."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22720,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Today our intrepid pair are jumping into a\nblack hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26360,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27360,
    "dDurationMs": 600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27960,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, to determine the fundamental structure\nof spacetime and its connection to quantum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32200,
    "dDurationMs": 8000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "entanglement of course."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40200,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In recent and less recent episodes we’ve\nseen how thinking about black holes leads"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44960,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to weird ideas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46600,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like the fact that there's a minimum meaningful\ndistance in space or that all of the information"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51480,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of a volume of space fits on its boundary."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54440,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We also saw a simplistic manner in which an\nentire new spatial dimension can actually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58960,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be encoded on that boundary, leading to the\nnotion of the holographic universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63680,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We even saw one idea for how gravity\ncould emerge from the thermodynamics on that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68520,
    "dDurationMs": 600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "boundary."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69120,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In a couple of recent episodes we talked about\nhow the emergent dimension could be encoded"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74680,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the scale of patterns on the boundary,\nbut these days most physicists working in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79600,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that area think there’s a better way to\ndo that encoding—and that’s with quantum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83520,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "entanglement—the subtle correlations between\nthe bits of quantum information that define"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89000,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the properties of particles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91240,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, as we’ll see in upcoming episodes,\nit’s starting to look like the entire fabric"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95880,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of space may be emergent from entanglement—that\nspace is sort of knit together from the network"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101960,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of mutual information of its contents."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105320,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This idea of the role of entanglement came\nfrom thinking about black holes in parallel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110320,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the stuff that led to the minimal Planck\nlength and the holographic principle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115320,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In particular, in thinking about what happens\nto quantum information in a black hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119960,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is ultimately going to lead us to a deep\nconnection between entanglement and wormholes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125680,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the ER=EPR conjecture."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128520,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that same line of reasoning is going to\ncompletely mess with our intuition about where"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134120,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quantum information exists, leading to black\nhole complementarity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139360,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We’ll get to these in upcoming episodes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141160,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But today we want to set up the contradiction\nthat drives all of this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145840,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And for that we need Alice and Bob to jump\ninto a black hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149480,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, just Alice actually."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151480,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "She always was a bit more adventurous than\nBob."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155720,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, Alice and Bob head to Sagittarius A*,\nthe supermassive black hole at the center"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160960,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the Milky Way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162320,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Alice suits up and prepares to jump."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164800,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bob prepares to watch from a safe distance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167600,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Alice carries a clock that emits pulses of\nhigh-energy gamma rays with a regular period"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172320,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that Bob can track her position and also\nobserve how her flow of time changes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177520,
    "dDurationMs": 6520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Alice also carries a box in which a single\nelectron has its spin frozen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184040,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is our qubit—our bit of quantum information."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187800,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this case the information is about whether\nthat electron spin is pointing up or down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192480,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The box also emits regular pulses of gamma\nrays so it can be tracked independently."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197600,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Excited to be the first human to see below\nan event horizon, Alice high-fives Bob and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201960,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leaps head-first towards Sag A*, and as she\nbegins her descent she throws the qubit box"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207640,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to fall just ahead of her."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209840,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let’s start with Bob’s perspective."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211960,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He watches Alice and box fall, training his\ngamma-ray telescope on them to monitor their"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216520,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "flow of time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217920,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those gamma ray photons arrive with increasing\nseparation due to gravitational time dilation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224200,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and at the same time the \nphotons are gravitationally "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226480,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "redshifted—stretched to longer wavelengths."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229480,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bob has also switched on detectors sensitive\nto all wavelengths from X-ray to visible to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234360,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "radio."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235360,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He settles in, expecting to watch Alice slow\ndown as she approaches the event horizon,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240680,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to witness her seconds stretched to hours,\nyears, millenia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246320,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That doesn’t happen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248080,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, he observes Alice fall quickly, speed\nup, and then suddenly slow down and merge"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253440,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the black hole’s event horizon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255080,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what happened to the time dilation approaching\ninfinity at the event horizon?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260840,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well it’s true that for any black hole you\ncan find a distance from the event horizon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266440,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with any ridiculously high time dilation you\nwant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270040,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like, a millisecond stretching to 100 trillion\nyears."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273760,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the thing is, a free-falling observer\nlike Alice is moving very very fast by the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279320,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time she reaches these points—she’s approaching\nthe speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283200,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The time dilation increases but the amount\nof time spent at each point decreases."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289040,
    "dDurationMs": 8360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ultimately, the former wins and both Alice’s\nand the box’s descent seem to slow and freeze—but"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297400,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only really really close to the event horizon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 300800,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bob sees the box slow and freeze first, which\nmeans Alice appears to catch up to the box."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306080,
    "dDurationMs": 7480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And Alice's head slows before her feet, so\nfrom Bob’s perspective she appears to flatten."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313560,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bob had been worried about \nthe opposite effect—that "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316600,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Alice might get spaghettified—elongated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319600,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by tidal forces pulling on her head harder\nthan her feet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323080,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that doesn’t happen here because the\nhuman-scale tidal forces for a black hole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 327520,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this massive are only deep inside of the hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331440,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, by the time the top of Alice’s\nhead is just above the event horizon, her"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336840,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "entire body is also just above the event horizon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340520,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This effect doesn’t have a term, but Bob\nwonders if pancakification might be appropriate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347240,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At this point, Alice’s photons are much\nfainter than the cosmic microwave background,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353600,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and their wavelengths much longer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356480,
    "dDurationMs": 7080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They’re barely detectable even by Bob’s\ngiant radio antenna."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363560,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then Bob loses sight altogether."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366760,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The last thing he sees is that all of Alice’s\nqubits along with the experimental qubit get"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 372160,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scrambled over the entire event horizon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374600,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now any light from Alice is indistinguishable\nfrom the black hole’s own Hawking radiation—and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380680,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "may be equivalent to it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382440,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hawking radiation is the faint glow that every "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385280,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "black hole produces due to \nits non-zero temperature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388280,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For Sag A* that temperature is 10^-14 Kelvin,\nresulting in Hawking photons with wavelengths"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395800,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of over 100 million kilometers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398160,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bob’s is desperate to not lose track of\nthe experimental qubit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401920,
    "dDurationMs": 6600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the only way is to collect all future\nHawking radiation emitted by the black hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408520,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He begins the construction of a detector that\nwill surround the entire black hole—a type"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413000,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Dyson sphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414920,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He also goes ahead and uploads his mind to\nthe ship’s computer so that he can outlive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418360,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this black hole, and he settles in for the\nlong game."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422000,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the meantime, let’s look at what happened\nto Alice from her own perspective."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426680,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Plummeting towards Sag A* takes some hours,\nbut that’s mostly far from the event horizon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432800,
    "dDurationMs": 5900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "She rapidly accelerates and the latter part\nof the journey wizzes by exponentially quickly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 438700,
    "dDurationMs": 6900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there’s no g-force from that acceleration\nand no tidal forces from the black hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445600,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Alice is in freefall towards an event horizon\nvastly larger than she is, so she feels like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451280,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "she’s floating."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452880,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a consequence of Einstein’s equivalence\nprinciple, which tells us that for an observer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456800,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in freefall, their local patch of spacetime\nbehaves exactly like space in the absence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461960,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of a gravitational field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464360,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Alice sees the black hole beneath her as a\nvast black surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469080,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oddly, that surface appears to move away from\nher as she approaches."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 473760,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See, the “true” event horizon looks black\nfrom a great distance due to the infinite"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479120,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gravitational redshift of photons struggling\nto depart it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483080,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That redshift results from the full trajectory\nout of the black hole’s gravitational well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489040,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Alice can still encounter photons that\nwere emitted a hair above the event horizon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 493760,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because she’s deep in that gravitational\nwell."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496200,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Effectively, she’s coming to them rather\nthan waiting for them to reach her."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500960,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Also, as Alice approaches the event horizon,\nher own extreme velocity sort of de-redshifts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507440,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the outward-pointing photons that she passes\nthrough."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510360,
    "dDurationMs": 6760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "She sees the record of objects that fell ahead\nof her, including the qubit box."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517120,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now comes the critical part of the experiment\nfrom Alice’s perspective."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521160,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At some point the qubit box crosses the true\nevent horizon ahead of her, even if she sees"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 526400,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no marker of that horizon in her reference\nframe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 530600,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Will she still see the box?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533520,
    "dDurationMs": 800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 534320,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the box she sees is the box as it was\njust before crossing the horizon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 539720,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "She can only catch photons emitted by the "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542200,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "box from below the horizon if \nshe crosses that horizon herself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547520,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "She is first and foremost"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 549040,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a scientist, so turns her mind back to the\nexperiment and plummets through the event"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553600,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "horizon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554800,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And nothing weird happens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556640,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Remember the equivalence principle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558120,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It tells us that there’s no experiment you\ncan do or observation you can make on the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 562120,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "local patch of space that distinguishes whether\nthat patch is freefalling or free-floating."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 567760,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This principle is the \nbedrock of general relativity "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570000,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and physicists are very uncomfortable by anything"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572440,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that appears to violate it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574480,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Remember this because we may have to break\nthis later, and it should make you uncomfortable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580040,
    "dDurationMs": 640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580680,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But assuming the equivalence principle holds,\nAlice can’t see things freeze at the event"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585360,
    "dDurationMs": 640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "horizon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 586000,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not the qubit, not herself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587880,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nor does she catch up to the qubit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590600,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now beneath the horizon, the qubit is still\nbelow her and gaining ground towards the dark"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596520,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "surface that also always appears below."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600200,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now that dark surface \nis growing and stretching "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603640,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around behind her also."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606000,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The outside universe is a shrinking fisheye\nview above—Alice’s sense of “up” irises"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613200,
    "dDurationMs": 7760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "closed, and all directions become an enveloping\n“down”, leading to a terminus of space"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620960,
    "dDurationMs": 840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 621800,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Alice can’t ever leave to tell Bob the result\nof the experiment, but from her perspective"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627280,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it’s a huge success."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629080,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "She now knows with surety that black holes\ncan swallow quantum bits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 634240,
    "dDurationMs": 1160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let’s go back to Bob."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635400,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Remember he’s now in the business of catching\nHawking radiation and looking for signs of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 639120,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the experimental qubit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641080,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Though if we’re being honest he’s also\nlooking for signs of Alice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 645640,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The black hole radiates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 647720,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It would lose mass this way if it were for\nthe fact that it eats more cosmic microwave"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652280,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "background than it spews up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 654240,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But after 100 billion years or so the universe\nhas expanded enough to dim the CMB below the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 659880,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "temperature of the black hole, and finally\nSagittarius A* starts to shrink, assuming"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 665240,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it doesn’t eat anything else."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667720,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bob is aware that the black hole will eventually\ncompletely evaporate through this radiation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672760,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He’s also aware of the law of conservation\nof quantum information and the black hole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677080,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "information paradox from watching ancient\nPBS Space Time episodes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681480,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He knows that quantum mechanics and perhaps\nhis own heart won’t allow the erasure of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686440,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Alice’s information nor the experimental\nqubit from the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691120,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there's a risk of that happening if the\nblack hole evaporates to nothing, and so,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695280,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just like many long-dead 21st century physicists,\nBob concludes that the information must be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700560,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hidden in the Hawking radiation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703320,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Many lifetimes of the universe pass and the \nHawking radiation appears completely random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 709360,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bob has had to build several \nstar-sized computers—Matryoshka "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713480,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "brains—to store and analyze this data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716840,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No big deal really because Bob \nhas nothing but time on his hands."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721400,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After the black hole has lost half of its\nmass—10^87 years later, when incidentally"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728040,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all the stars have gone out and their stellar\nremnants have scattered to the void."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732280,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s now just Bob and the black hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 735040,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then Bob analyzes the next in the endless stream\nof information-barren Hawking radiation, but"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742560,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this time he detects the first sign of a faint\npattern."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 748040,
    "dDurationMs": 6840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The subtlest of correlation starts to emerge\nbetween all past radiation, hinting at some"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 754880,
    "dDurationMs": 8000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "profoundly scrambled order in the randomness\nof the bits stuck on the black hole event horizon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 762880,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Newly excited by his Sisophean task, Bob continues\nto collect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 767720,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Eventually he managed to recovers the object "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 769880,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the experiment—quantum \nbit, proving incontrovertibly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 774600,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that black holes do NOT \nswallow quantum information."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778280,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And just before the black hole evaporates\nentirely, Bob also recovers all bits that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 782680,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were once Alice, revealing the true source\nof his long patience."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 786680,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He brings to bear the full might of the enormous "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 788840,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "black-hole-powered Matryoska \nbrains and reverse-engineers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792360,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all of Alice’s qubits to reconstructs her\nconsciousness in digital form and the two"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 796880,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "live happily ever after, digital ghosts in\na dead universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 801360,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How sweet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 803320,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This might seem like a happy ending, and it\nis for Bob and for the version of Alice encoded"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 808120,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the event horizon, but not necessarily\nfor the version that fell in, nor for physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 815800,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let’s get back to our experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 817560,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What really happened to the qubit?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819640,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bob saw it freeze on the horizon, and then\neventually catches it when it emerged as Hawking"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824800,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "radiation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 826200,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Alice saw it fall through the horizon and\nthen merge with the singularity just before"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 830440,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "she did the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 831840,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In physics, we often make progress by identifying\ncontradictions in a theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 835840,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is perhaps the primary \nvalue of the gerdankenexperiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840240,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it seems we’ve identified a contradiction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 842280,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Two different observers end up with irreconcilably\ndifferent answers to the question “where"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 848040,
    "dDurationMs": 1160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the qubit”."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 849200,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There’s a reason we used a qubit instead\nof just asking, for example, where is Alice?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854240,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’s because the qubit allows us to break\nvery specific rules in quantum mechanics and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 859080,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it sharpens our contradiction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 861440,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I already talked about the prohibition against\ndeleting quantum information, which is why"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 866160,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bob concluded that the qubit had to be preserved\nin Hawking radiation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 871080,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there’s another related rule—the no-cloning\ntheorem states that quantum bits can’t be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 876160,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "duplicated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 877680,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the bit escapes in Hawking radiation, how\ncan it also be inside the black hole?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 882720,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem with deleting or duplicating quantum\ninformation is that it breaks what may be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 887080,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the most fundamental tenet of quantum mechanics—as\nfoundational as the equivalence principle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 892600,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is to general relativity—and that’s unitarity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 897160,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The quantum wavefunction describes probabilities."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 899720,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Probabilities have to add up to one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 902080,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Add up all the probabilities of an object's\npossible position and they can’t add up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 906600,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to more than 100%—because what would that\neven mean?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 910360,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Deleting or duplicating a qubit breaks unitarity,\nand so is a no-no."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 914840,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it seems we have to either break unitarity\nby duplicating the qubit in the Hawking radiation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920600,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or by deleting it as the black hole evaporates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 924240,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "OR we have to break the equivalence principle\nby saying that Alice and her bit never get"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 929760,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "past the event horizon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 931760,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To find out which is the case, you’re going\nto have to wait another week."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 935760,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Remember, Bob waited 10^87 years—a week\nisn’t so bad."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939920,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then we’ll start to see some of the possible\nsolutions to this paradox, from black hole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 945400,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "complementarity to idea of the firewall at\nthe event horizon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 950040,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we’ll continue to sharpen the tools\nwe need to knit entangled qubits into the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 956280,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "very fabric of spacetime."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 958680,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey Everybody. Before we go we wanted to let you \nknow we have two new limited edition Merch items  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 964240,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up at the Merch store. First up is our first ever \nBlack Hole Enamel pin. This is a 1.5 inch enamel  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 971240,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pin on 2x3 inch holo foil backing card designed \nby the Space Time gfx team. These pins are limited  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 978360,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "edition pre-sale with the pins shipping during \nthe second week of June. Once we’re out of stock  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 983640,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the pre-sale, that’s it. Next up is our Star \nWars inspired Space Time t-shirt and sweatshirt.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 990000,
    "dDurationMs": 3429,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Designed by our very star wars nerdy director, \nyou can now express your love and knowledge of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 993429,
    "dDurationMs": 6451,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the force. This limited edition design will be \navailable until May The 4th. To put your order in,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 999880,
    "dDurationMs": 18960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just head over pbsspacetime.com/shop \nor click the link the description."
    } ]
  } ]
}
